# Registration Data Integration Walkthrough

I have ensured that all information collected during registration (Sector, Email, Job Title, Department, etc.) is correctly saved and displayed on the profile page.

## Key Changes

### 1. Updated Profile UI
- **Added Sector Field**: The Professional Information tab on the profile page now includes a "Sector" dropdown (Oil & Gas, Energy, Manufacturing) to match the registration form.
- **Enhanced Data Mapping**: Fixed the "Organization" field to correctly map to the `orgName` database column.
- **Comprehensive Population**: The profile page now automatically populates all fields with data provided during registration, including Email, Job Title, Department, Phone, Location, and Bio.

### 2. Backend Enhancements
- **server.js**: 
    - Updated the `/api/users/:id` PUT endpoint to include the `sector` column in updates.
    - Improved naming flexibility to handle both `company` (frontend) and `orgName` (backend/DB) naming conventions seamlessly.

### 3. Logic Improvements
- **Automatic Display**: The profile hero section now uses the user's `sector` as a default role if no Job Title is provided.
- **Persistent Updates**: All fields, including the new Sector field, are now correctly persisted to the database and localStorage when you save your profile.

## How to use
1.  Register a new account and fill in the "Professional Profile" section.
2.  Log in and navigate to the **Profile** page.
3.  You will see all your registration details pre-filled in the Personal and Professional tabs.
4.  Updates made on the profile page will now correctly include your Sector choice.

